    {
      "id": "h-monitoring-after-mitigation",
      "title": "H. Monitoring after mitigation",
      "prose": [
        "Google’s Site Reliability Engineering guidance identifies four foundational service-health signals: latency, traffic, errors and saturation. For banking, add financial correctness and customer impact.",
        "A strong answer identifies incident ownership, the action that contains further harm, the conditions for recovery, and any permanent fix. Useful post-incident outputs are root-cause analysis, quantified customer impact, corrective actions, monitoring improvements and a prevention owner."
      ],
